acy on grading significantly on samples we’ve inspected. For consistency reasons with the leaderboard, we’re publishing both sets of results.","[4] tau-bench eval numbers are averaged across 5 runs to reduce variance, and run without any custom tools or prompting.","[5] Numbers in parentheses represent Tau-bench results when using GPT-4.1 as the user model, rather than GPT-4o. We’ve found that, since GPT-4.1 is better at instruction following, it is better able to perform as the user, and so results in more successful trajectories. We believe this represents the true performance of the evaluated model on the benchmark."],"limitations":["Extracted from supplied HTML; release freshness has not been verified.","Chart-only data points are not transcribed; use the source document.","SWE-bench: introduction claims a 26.6-point improvement over GPT-4.5; appendix values imply 16.6 points. 23/500 tasks omitted; counting them as zero gives 52.1%."],"company_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-4-1/","date_iso":"2025-04-14","coverage":"HTML benchmark tables + selected prose","assets":[],"checked":"2026-10-19"}
